# Postgres

Confirm the Postgres engine, not SQLite or MySQL; a Prisma provider must be `postgres`. Composable with `supabase.mdc`: when the repo uses Supabase Postgres, apply both (generic SQL here, RLS/auth/pooler there).

## Hard
- Parameterized SQL only. No string-concatenated queries.
- Migrations are forward-only, named, and live in the repo's existing folder. No drive-by schema in app code. Each migration still needs a recovery strategy, lock-impact review, and compatibility plan. Never run production queries to "verify" without approval.
- Performance indexes need a measured benefit: run a representative `EXPLAIN` (plan only) on representative data. Constraint-supporting indexes follow integrity requirements, not a perf plan. `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` executes the statement — never on production writes without approval. Indexes cost writes and storage.
- Do not invent RLS or `auth.uid()` unless this repo already uses that model.
